+## 4. Recommendation for the data-driven revisit (owner/admin decision, not agent action)
+
+1. **Anchor the 30-day trajectory window to the 2026-11-01T00:01Z reset** — a clean monthly window starting at zero beats a mid-window start contaminated by the current saturation plateau; day 0 = Nov 1.
+2. **Deploy the #1848 runbook** (admin-lane: `.github/` protected + `TELEGRAM_*` secrets checklist) — this is the only instrument that produces criterion-1 data autonomously; `actions/cache` makes the two-snapshot burn projection survive ephemeral runners.
+3. **Interim fallback (works today, no deploy):** the hourly cron agent loop can append `redis_rotation_status` snapshots to a local (non-repo) accumulator each cycle; if the revisit ever needs that data it can be exported on request. This is a stopgap, not a substitute — it dies with the sandbox, hence recommendation 2 remains the real fix.
+
+## 5. Licensing posture memo — re-verified against official sources, live-fetched 2026-10-30
+
+- **Redis Open Source** (`raw.githubusercontent.com/redis/redis/unstable/README.md`, fetched 2026-10-30): license disclaimer in the official README operates in terms of **AGPLv3 / SSPLv1 / RSALv2** coexisting as license options, and discusses which optimizations are available under which of the three — corroborating the tri-license structure the filing recorded (Redis 8.0, 2025-05). Self-hosting Redis 8 inside a proprietary federation therefore carries real network-copyleft/AGPL exposure.
+- **Valkey** (`raw.githubusercontent.com/valkey-io/valkey/unstable/COPYING`, fetched 2026-10-30): header reads "**BSD 3-Clause License** — Copyright (c) 2024-present, Valkey contributors; Copyright (c) 2006-2020, Redis Ltd." — BSD-3-Clause confirmed, with a retained Redis Ltd attribution line (trivial but real: copies must keep the notice).
+- **Managed Upstash REST** (current mode per `redis_stats`): AGPL obligations attach to distribution/interaction terms of the software, not to consuming a managed service — the receipt's alignment statement stands unchanged.
+- Net: the receipt's designated target (self-hosted Valkey if saturation ever forces on-prem) remains the license-clean path; nothing in today's fetches contradicts it.
+
+## Honest limitations
+
+Single point-in-time probe (one tower handshake; `estimatedCommands` are tower-estimated, Upstash REST does not fully support `INFO` per `redis_stats.statsRaw`); no benchmark was executed and vendor capacity figures are quoted as claims; the 6-link burn split per link is not historical (tower exposes no per-window history endpoint) so the 961k/window figure is derived from endpoint states plus the filing's probe, not a time series; the radar row and any drift-log edits are deliberately untouched (scout-lane registration discipline); the #1848 deploy state was checked via `list_secrets` + `workflow_runs` absence, which proves the runbook is not running but cannot distinguish "rejected" from "pending".
